NOTICE

hermes-eva-theme is a port of a DeepSeek Harness plugin to Hermes Desktop.
Three kinds of material end up in the same folder, and they do not share a
licence.

1. Port code — this repository
   MIT. See LICENSE. Covers build/build.mjs, src/body.js, the generated
   plugin/plugin.js, docs/ and the README.

2. Upstream plugin — seaison/dsh-plugin-eva-theme
   MIT code, https://github.com/seaison/dsh-plugin-eva-theme
   Ported at commit f8b9638 ("docs: refresh README showcase and v0.51.2
   installation guide", v0.51.2).

   What this port takes from it:
   - the 107-entry PALETTE table (every colour value in plugin/plugin.js)
   - the boot-sequence design (NERV card, emergency alarm, pilot select,
     plug sync, doors) and its copy
   - the scanline, Mincho-heading and hairline styling intent
   - file layout conventions for its assets/ folder

   What it does not take: the cordis host API, the DSH CSS Modules selectors,
   the now-playing player, the balance proxy and the osascript track control.
   Those have no Hermes equivalent or were dropped by decision (see the
   repository's docs and the porting notes).

   The upstream MIT licence text applies to that code; keep its copyright and
   permission notice with any redistribution of the derived parts.

3. Media — third-party, not distributed here
   The plugin references these assets at runtime, but this repository does not
   ship them, and the MIT licence above does not apply to them:

   - character line art and avatars (Asuka, Rei)
   - voice clips
   - the NERV boot animation and the NERV / emergency / entry-plug SVGs
   - the original sound track, if a user adds one

   They carry their own terms (the upstream repository's NOTICE.md and
   docs/assets.md describe them). Treat them as local, personal use only: do
   not publish a package, archive or repository that contains them, and do not
   use them commercially.

   To run the plugin you supply them yourself: build from an upstream checkout
   (see README) or drop your own files into media-src/ under the exact names
   listed in media-src/README.md.

